WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.870 --> 00:00:05.109
Charlie will be disappointed to hear that
his Angels didn't make it to Box Office Heaven

00:00:05.109 --> 00:00:06.710
this past weekend.

00:00:06.710 --> 00:00:12.049
According to Deadline, the film suffered a
dismal $8.6 million domestic opening, and

00:00:12.049 --> 00:00:17.180
it only earned a paltry $27.9 million internationally
across 26 markets.

00:00:17.180 --> 00:00:23.140
Beyond that, the film had an especially poor
opening in China, making just $7.8 million

00:00:23.140 --> 00:00:25.400
in the lucrative overseas territory.

00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:27.560
So what went wrong, exactly?

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:30.410
Charlie's Angels seemed to have a whole lot
going for it.

00:00:30.410 --> 00:00:36.220
The film stars indie darling Kristen Stewart,
up-and-comer Ella Balinska, Aladdin star Naomi

00:00:36.220 --> 00:00:40.989
Scott, and the always welcome Elizabeth Banks,
who also directed the caper.

00:00:40.989 --> 00:00:45.179
Even the formidable presence of Patrick Stewart
wasn't quite enough to help this film.

00:00:45.179 --> 00:00:49.500
Well, according to Deadline, the lousy box
office was at least partially due to issues

00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:54.859
with the script, which reportedly underwent
numerous changes during development and production.

00:00:54.859 --> 00:00:59.660
There were apparently certain pain points
in the storyline that just couldn't be fixed…even

00:00:59.660 --> 00:01:01.570
with lots of rewrites.

00:01:01.570 --> 00:01:06.130
And it sounds like this clunker of a script
was a major turn-off to some A-list stars.

00:01:06.130 --> 00:01:07.380
As Deadline reports,

00:01:07.380 --> 00:01:11.420
"The script for Charlie’s Angels didn’t
really attract top talent [like] Jennifer

00:01:11.420 --> 00:01:15.870
Lawrence, Emma Stone and Margot Robbie (a
trio that would have potentially jazzed up

00:01:15.870 --> 00:01:16.870
business)."

00:01:16.870 --> 00:01:21.200
Instead, Sony brass chose two relative fresh
faces to star alongside Stewart.

00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:26.060
However, Balinska and Scott might have been
a little too fresh-faced for general audiences.

00:01:26.060 --> 00:01:29.710
The fact that they aren't quite household
names turned out to be a detriment rather

00:01:29.710 --> 00:01:31.280
than a drawing point.

00:01:31.280 --> 00:01:35.000
As Deadline reports, Stewart herself may have
caused the film to flop:

00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:39.840
"Stewart, who is hysterical in the movie and
even needed more funny bits, is in a different

00:01:39.840 --> 00:01:43.170
place in her career professionally, publicly,
and privately.

00:01:43.170 --> 00:01:47.560
It’s unfair to think that she could deliver
her Twilight fans now."

00:01:47.560 --> 00:01:52.490
After years of appearing in arthouse films
and relatively low-key projects, it's indeed

00:01:52.490 --> 00:01:56.980
unlikely that Stewart would be able to bring
huge crowds to a film like Charlie's Angels,

00:01:56.980 --> 00:02:00.980
especially when she's paired with new faces
like Balinska and Scott.

00:02:00.980 --> 00:02:06.530
But the film's grim box office can't be blamed
entirely on Stewart and her fellow Angels.

00:02:06.530 --> 00:02:11.489
The film's action sequences were admittedly
lackluster…a fact that seemed clear even

00:02:11.489 --> 00:02:12.840
in the film's trailers.

00:02:12.840 --> 00:02:17.780
And here's another question: Did anyone even
want a new Charlie's Angels movie?

00:02:17.780 --> 00:02:18.780
According to Deadline:

00:02:18.780 --> 00:02:23.680
"After [Elizabeth Banks] expressed interest...in
taking on a Charlie’s Angels reboot with

00:02:23.680 --> 00:02:28.159
a modern feminist spin, there was no question
in Sony’s mind that the project should move

00:02:28.159 --> 00:02:29.159
forward."

00:02:29.159 --> 00:02:34.409
Sure, it's been quite a few years since Lucy
Liu, Cameron Diaz, and Drew Barrymore twerked

00:02:34.409 --> 00:02:38.329
across movie screens in their own Charlie's
Angels films, but that doesn't mean we were

00:02:38.329 --> 00:02:41.129
all champing at the bit for a brand-new installment.

00:02:41.129 --> 00:02:45.569
In the wake of Charlie's Angels' less-than-stellar
performance, don't be surprised to see a bunch

00:02:45.569 --> 00:02:50.390
of think pieces claiming that female-led movies
don't bring folks to the box office.

00:02:50.390 --> 00:02:52.150
That clearly isn't true.

00:02:52.150 --> 00:02:56.719
After all, Hustlers was a bonafide hit, and
it premiered to great returns in September

00:02:56.719 --> 00:02:57.719
2019.

00:02:57.719 --> 00:03:02.459
Based on a true story, the film involves a
bunch of New York City dancers who bilk Wall

00:03:02.459 --> 00:03:04.889
Street bankers out of their fortunes.

00:03:04.889 --> 00:03:10.029
Fronted by an all-female cast and created
by a predominantly female creative team, Hustlers

00:03:10.029 --> 00:03:15.390
earned an impressive $33 million on its domestic
opening weekend, marking the largest opening

00:03:15.390 --> 00:03:18.310
of Jennifer Lopez's storied acting career.

00:03:18.310 --> 00:03:23.790
There's absolutely no doubt that movies created
by women and starring women can and will succeed

00:03:23.790 --> 00:03:24.790
at the box office.

00:03:24.790 --> 00:03:29.849
In the end, the issues with Charlie's Angels
may have been rooted solely in its script

00:03:29.849 --> 00:03:34.639
and production, but the middling 58 percent
rating on Rotten Tomatoes certainly didn't

00:03:34.639 --> 00:03:35.640
help matters.

00:03:35.640 --> 00:03:39.829
Still, it's disappointing that the film is
financially floundering.

00:03:39.829 --> 00:03:44.480
Stars like Stewart and Banks will undoubtedly
survive this career blip, and hopefully Balinska

00:03:44.480 --> 00:03:48.189
and Scott will soon be given meatier roles
to sink their teeth into.

00:03:48.189 --> 00:03:49.189
And who knows?

00:03:49.189 --> 00:03:53.930
Perhaps movie execs will take a cue from Charlie's
Angels and realize that some franchises just

00:03:53.930 --> 00:03:57.950
don't need to be rebooted, remade, or otherwise
freshened up.

00:03:57.950 --> 00:03:58.950
"Mints."

00:03:58.950 --> 00:04:00.959
"Let's just stop the touching.

00:04:00.959 --> 00:04:02.659
Some of these blows up."

